    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95371.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "Of course it is a very different world now and fracking in Colorado of course is very controversial and it's certainly more controversial than other states in the West because it's here where we have this type of production coming face to face with major populations. Now this has led to handfuls of potential ballot measures slated to perhaps gather signatures for this November's ballot. You worked hard to try to craft a compromise legislation to provide some sort of local control to communities in a way that was a compromise with industry as well. That effort failed in the waning days of the legislative session this year, why?",
