  {
    "episode_id": 95371,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95371.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, you look around the state. So the organizations we've heard from a variety of chambers of commerce and other business organizations, home builders, I mean, various industries. are very concerned about this ballot initiative. Any of these would pass. They think it could dramatically hurt the economy. And they are determined that they would raise a lot of money and put millions of dollars into TV ads. And I think the folks that are supporting for the setback, like a larger setback or the local control, they're going to go out and raise a lot of money. I think both sides would prefer not to have to spend their money on TV ads for an initiative that has an uncertain outcome. So it really, when you're looking at up to $30 million might be spent on this kind of an initiative, that's a lot of money that could be used better elsewhere.",
